Then again, Pol Pot more or less tried that, didn't he?

Myself, I care more about my own well being than that of the snail
darter. I honestly could care less if all the snail darters in the
world were killed so that I could have a choice of prepackaged meals.
Its obviously in my interest that the planet remain habitable, but its
not obvious to me that preserving the gnat catcher will be needed to
do that. I'm far more interested in modern laundry detergent and
washing machines -- they keep my clothes clean without my having to
spend hours of backbreaking labor every week on washing them, which
was what our ancestors had to do.

